<title>USA: Drypers Corp Q3 shr profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Drypers Corp Q3 shr profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr profit		 $0.12     loss	 $0.40</p>
<p> Net profit		 1,956     loss	 2,656</p>
<p> Sales		     55,066		   43,295</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  16,119		    6,601</p>
<p>	  9  MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr loss		   $0.15     loss	 $1.84</p>
<p> Net loss		     611     loss	12,071</p>
<p> Sales		    152,929		  117,393</p>
<p> Avg shrs		   6,640		    6,574</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE - Q3 1995 average shares include nine million common shares issuable upon conversion of 90,000 shares of convertible preferred shares issued in February 1996. The company said that given the loss for the nine months ended September 30, 1996, such common stock equivalents have not been included since the effect would be antidilutive.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
